 * SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause
 *
 * Reserves zero-filled space at the EXACT MRAM address declared in
 * manifest.json for one Wi-Fi ROM patch blob.
 *
 * Two purposes:
 *   1. LINKER GUARD — if app code or data grows into this address range
 *      the linker emits a section overlap error immediately.
 *   2. FOTA correctness — inject_wifi_patch.py fills the zero reservation
 *      before imgtool signs, so zephyr.signed.bin carries the patch bytes
 *      at the correct binary offset.  When MCUboot swaps slot1→slot0 the
 *      patches land at exactly lmac_origin / umac_origin in MRAM.
 *
 * Note: with patches at 0x100000+ the binary offset from slot0_start is
 * ~960 KB — far beyond the MCUboot header zone (bytes 0..0x7FF).
 * imgtool check_header() is therefore never triggered.
 */

.@section_name@ @patch_origin@ (READONLY) :
{
    . = . + @patch_size@;
} > FLASH = 0
